{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8yMDIxL0RyaW5rd2F0ZXIlMjAlMjgyMDIxJTI5Lw","type":"movie","name":"Drinkwater","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/zfeHyfkG5OxAC0wlcbh8cPGIFlt.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/nIzAK2g8yZTNSM0yfzlceqc11sV.jpg","description":"In small-town British Columbia, Canada, awkward teen Mike Drinkwater has trouble fitting in and is bullied by his antagonist and rival: wealthy school jock, Luke Ryan. While Mike's offbeat father, Hank, spends more time defrauding the government than being a role model; Hank is dealing with his own longstanding condemnation by Luke's father Wesley Ryan, which seems to fuel Luke's hostility towards Mike. Enter Wallace, a young girl from the United States who is adjusting to life in a new place while recovering from her own personal tragedy. Wallace's strength of character helps transform her life and the lives of the people around her.","releaseInfo":"2021","genres":["Comedy","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"5.9","runtime":"112 min","cast":["Eric McCormack","Daniel Doheny","Louriza Tronco","Jordan Burtchett","Alex Zahara","Bob Frazer","Naika Toussaint","Linda Darlow"],"director":["Stephen S. Campanelli"],"released":"2022-10-14T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"Canada. The 80s. All the good stuff, eh?","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Eric McCormack","character":"Hank Drinkwater","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/nAVgJZeptg0ay0adsYhnrGf9Jsc.jpg"},{"name":"Daniel Doheny","character":"Mike Drinkwater","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/wRmWiPx9X2IozM0EZNeOHs2VT18.jpg"},{"name":"Louriza Tronco","character":"Wallace Owens","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/taqxXukoTRHmn6SieJwOys91QaF.jpg"},{"name":"Jordan Burtchett","character":"Luke Ryan","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/wXCUmxrCh9KJPTCPCIUCw83K2K1.jpg"},{"name":"Alex Zahara","character":"Mr. Babcock","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/8T6k1sBrWyLI368Mk9iyYuwpqv2.jpg"},{"name":"Bob Fr